I think this call is redundant here.
Also additional constructor `DAILY_STATS(int){}` is not necessary too.
when making `static const DAILY_STATS x;` all members of this struct will be implicitly initialized ( https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/language/initialization#Implicit_initialization )
So from my prospective, double initialization (ok, double clean) happens here.
I'd change the code to smth like this:
```
DAILY_STATS(){}
void clear() {
    static const DAILY_STATS x;
    *this = x;
}
```

